# [CSCS diagnostic, 2026-09-04] Rank-0 stall dumper for the delta_sharded STEADY sync.
#
# Run 3289420 (train-gsm8k-deepseek-v3-671B-v1-separate-async-megatron.sh): the first steady
# delta sync carrying real gradients hung for the full 30-min NCCL timeout. Flight recorder:
# 479 ranks waiting in the WORLD count all_gather (SeqNum=5); rank 0 (wire master) shows
# "Last enqueued NCCL work: 3, last completed 3" -- it completed the sub-round index gather and
# never enqueued the value gather that is the very next dist.gather call, i.e. it is stuck
# inside NCCL's launch of a 480-peer gather-to-one (delta_export.py routes every param over the
# WORLD group under PP>1). The recorder cannot show WHERE rank 0 sits. Same signature as GLM run
# 3263683. Diagnostic only, applied on top of delta-sharded-gather-round-size.patch.
#
# What it does: when rank 0 enters a steady send_weights, a daemon thread waits 600 s and then,
# while that thread is still inside send_weights, every 300 s prints all Python thread stacks
# (faulthandler) plus `py-spy dump --native` (falls back to a python-only dump) of this process
# to stderr, which Ray relays into the slurm log as [WSYNC-STALL] lines -- well before the
# 1800 s watchdog kills the job. Self-terminates when send_weights returns. Not applied on the
# other ranks (their state is known: blocked in the all_gather).
#
# Generated from a real git worktree at verl v0.9.0 + delta-sharded-gather-round-size.patch;
# git apply --check / py_compile / --reverse --check verified. MUST be applied AFTER
# delta-sharded-gather-round-size.patch (same file).
